# Shared UI Conventions

- Keep primitives in `src/lib`.
- Keep composites in `src/components`.
- Promote module-specific UI into shared only after reuse in at least two module scopes.

## Required patterns

- Primitives stay generic and theme-driven.
- Composites avoid feature-specific business logic.
- Shared layers must remain consumable by `src/modules/*`.

## Prohibited patterns

- Feature data fetching directly inside generic UI primitives.
- App-wide layout assumptions hardcoded inside shared components.
- Imports from `src/modules/*` inside `src/components` or `src/lib`.
